# POM composition — the rules (full design: `docs/design-hint-architecture.md`)

**Core nodes have fixed syntax.** Table/Td, Ul/Li, Text, Chart, Timeline, Flow, Tree, Matrix, ProcessArrow, Pyramid (and items) are never extended. Richer visuals are derived components composed AROUND them with VStack/HStack (cards, KPI tiles, icon+text rows, card header icon). A table stays a table.

## Single sources of truth — never hardcode these elsewhere
- Nesting: `children:` in `src/knowledge/core/nodes.yaml` → enforced by `src/compiler/content_model.py`.
- What a design_hint may ask for, per component kind: `src/knowledge/core/hint-capabilities.yaml` → rendered by `src/agents/hint_capabilities.py` for the planner and the generator.
- Icon names: `src/knowledge/core/icon-names.txt` (generated by `scripts/export_icon_names.py`); curated prompt list in `src/knowledge/components/icon.yaml` `recommended_names`.

## Hard facts (POM v10.3.0)
- `<Text>`, `<Td>`, `<Li>` hold text + inline tags only (B, I, A, U, S, Sub, Sup, Span, Mark).
  HStack/Icon in `<Td>` → whole table fails with misleading `Missing required attribute "rows"`; Icon in `<Li>` → silently dropped.
- Unknown `<Icon name>` fails parseXml. Lucide has no brand logos.

## When changing code or prompts
- New nesting rule/node → `nodes.yaml` + test in `tests/unit/test_content_model.py`.
- New visual treatment → `hint-capabilities.yaml` only (tests check coverage + that technique snippets nest validly).
- New component kind → `planner_schema.ComponentKindLiteral` AND `hint-capabilities.yaml` `kinds:`.
- Never write a prompt recipe that nests layout/Icon/Shape/Chart inside a text-only or data node.
- Keep generator system prompt within `test_context_builder` budgets by making guidance per-slide/per-component, not by raising budgets.
- Nesting violations are blocking `INVALID_CHILD` and must skip the compiler (`nesting_compile_failure`) on every compile path.
